course: dictionary
lesson: 1449
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them tells you which one is meant. Cartwheel is one of these words. Read the clues before you choose.
explain: «Cartwheels and handstands at home are practised on grass or a mat, away from furniture.» Practised, grass, mat and handstands show that this is the gymnastics move. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: «Alice hears a rumbling of little cartwheels» is different. A rumbling means things rolling along, so here cartwheels are the wheels of a cart. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A cartwheel can be a gymnastics move: you put your hands down one after the other, swing your legs over your head in a circle, and land on your feet.
fact: A cartwheel can also be the wheel of a cart.
fact: To cartwheel means to do cartwheels, or to roll over and over sideways.
fact: Cartwheel is a noun and a verb. The past tense of the verb is cartwheeled, as in «She cartwheeled across the grass.»
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word. The context tells you which meaning is meant.
exercise: «Cartwheels and handstands at home are practised on grass or a mat, away from furniture.» Where is it safest to practise? | On the kitchen table | *On grass or a mat, away from furniture | On a icy road
exercise: «Alice hears a rumbling of little cartwheels and many voices.» What are the cartwheels here? | *The wheels of a cart | A gymnastics move | Parts of a clock | A kind of cake
exercise: «Mia did one in the playground to prove it.» What did Mia do? | *A cartwheel, a gymnastics move | A cake | A wheel of a bicycle
test: Which meaning of cartwheel is a gymnastics move? | A wheel with spokes made of wood | The wheel of a cart | *Hands down, legs swung over the head in a circle, landing on your feet
test: Yesterday Sam ___ across the field. | *cartwheeled | cartwheel | cartwheels | cartwheeling
exam: «In two weeks he does the whole cartwheel.» What does cartwheel mean here? | *A gymnastics move, with hands down and legs swung over the head | The wheel of a cart | A kind of cake | A ladder used to reach high shelves
